{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/977321-premade-adventures-for-chronicles-of-darkness","id":977321,"title":"Premade adventures for Chronicles of Darkness","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-09-27T12:58:04-07:00","id":977321,"title":"Premade adventures for Chronicles of Darkness","content":"Do there exist any official adventures/campaigns for the new Chronicles of Darkness? Not talking about old stuff for previous editions, I am new myself to this setting and would like to prevent any conversation chores of old material. And no Vampire, Werewolf and the like, just plain CoD material.<br /> It would be tremendously helpful for me to convince my group who are new to this Storyteller of this system. I want to present an intruiging entry and catch their interest.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-27T13:06:25-07:00","id":977327,"title":"","content":"While I don't think CofD has any yet, the 1e content (back when it was still New World of Darkness) had tons of stuff under the Storytelling Adventure System.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-27T13:06:48-07:00","id":977330,"title":"","content":"No. There's a vampire one, but if you're not counting vampire then no.<br /> <br /> However the mortal SAS' available for first edition are easily adapted for second.<br /> <br /> You can see some of them <a href=\"http://whitewolf.wikia.com/wiki/Storytelling_Adventure_System\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-27T13:25:09-07:00","id":977341,"title":"","content":"The God-Machine Chronicle and Chronicles of Darkness books have several adventures (they're the same across both books) written up assuming you're using mortals.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-27T13:36:01-07:00","id":977355,"title":"","content":"Both Demon and Beast include a short adventure in the back of their core books.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(he/him/his)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Backer #2010","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","name":"ElvesofZion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-27T14:05:08-07:00","id":977378,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BigDamnHero</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/977321-premade-adventures-for-chronicles-of-darkness?p=977341#post977341\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The God-Machine Chronicle and Chronicles of Darkness books have several adventures (they're the same across both books) written up assuming you're using mortals.</div> </div> </div> </div>Kind of. They're more story seeds than actual adventures.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-27T15:02:10-07:00","id":977420,"title":"","content":"If you're just looking for vanilla CoD material for human characters, your best bet would be the Chronicles of Darkness book which has no less than 20 adventure seeds of 2-3 pages each, including fully statted NPCs. You'll have to do a little bit of assembly and prep yourself, but they're solid hooks with useful details to build on.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-27T15:28:06-07:00","id":977429,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caladriu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/977321-premade-adventures-for-chronicles-of-darkness?p=977420#post977420\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you're just looking for vanilla CoD material for human characters, your best bet would be the Chronicles of Darkness book which has no less than 20 adventure seeds of 2-3 pages each, including fully statted NPCs. You'll have to do a little bit of assembly and prep yourself, but they're solid hooks with useful details to build on.</div> </div> </div> </div>Eh. If you're trying to sell a group on CofD on the basis of &quot;look at these cool pre-made adventures!&quot;, I don't think the story seeds in CofD/GMC are going to do it. They require a lot more work than a lot of groups looking for pre-made adventures are looking to do.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-27T18:48:39-07:00","id":977520,"title":"","content":"Unfortunately, there really are not very many pre-made adventures for CofD. None for 2nd Edition specifically, in fact. Luckily, it takes next to no work to convert the pre-made SAS adventures for 1st edition to 2nd. But there aren't a <i>whole lot</i> of those either, less for Vanilla. Sadly, pre-made adventures don't seem to be where the money is at, since by nature they're a GM-only product, so roughly five sixth of your target audience is actively discouraged from buying them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-27T19:06:59-07:00","id":977529,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/977321-premade-adventures-for-chronicles-of-darkness?p=977520#post977520\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Unfortunately, there really are not very many pre-made adventures for CofD. None for 2nd Edition specifically, in fact. Luckily, it takes next to no work to convert the pre-made SAS adventures for 1st edition to 2nd. But there aren't a <i>whole lot</i> of those either, less for Vanilla. Sadly, pre-made adventures don't seem to be where the money is at, since by nature they're a GM-only product, so roughly five sixth of your target audience is actively discouraged from buying them.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> in my group only the GM (me) buys the products, and I personally, actively dislike the lack of pre-made adventures or the downplayed focus on GM Material. If there's no GM, there is no game. If there is no game, no one is buying. I mean I wouldn't want a ton of them... but it'd be nice if each game got a tutorial adventure. I also wish the storytellers guides came before the player guides.<br /> <br /> Not sadly in this case, but Dark Eras is really just a bunch of seeds too, however it does contain a metric ton of options...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.pinterest.com/xenoterracide/chrod-inspirations/\" target=\"_blank\">Graphic Inspirational Photos for Chronicles of Darkness on Pinterest</a> <br /> <a href=\"https://chroniclesofdarkness.slack.com\" target=\"_blank\">Chronicles of Darkness Slack</a> (PM Me with Email for an Invite, then invite your friends)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4046-xenoterracide","name":"xenoterracide","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"563"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-27T19:12:35-07:00","id":977531,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>xenoterracide</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/977321-premade-adventures-for-chronicles-of-darkness?p=977529#post977529\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">in my group only the GM (me) buys the products, and I personally, actively dislike the lack of pre-made adventures or the downplayed focus on GM Material. If there's no GM, there is no game. If there is no game, no one is buying. I mean I wouldn't want a ton of them... but it'd be nice if each game got a tutorial adventure. I also wish the storytellers guides came before the player guides.<br /> <br /> Not sadly in this case, but Dark Eras is really just a bunch of seeds too, however it does contain a metric ton of options...</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I agree. I would really like to see more SAS adventures again.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-27T22:57:21-07:00","id":977615,"title":"","content":"There's the Quickstart for each 2E line that has one:<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/114063/Reap-the-Whirlwind?cPath=8329_20642\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a><br /> <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/118271/Demon-The-Descent-Quickstart?manufacturers_id=4261\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a><br /> <br /> Huh, I thought there were more of them? Guess not <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1462-xenesis","name":"Xenesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1462_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-28T07:02:43-07:00","id":977739,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Xenesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/977321-premade-adventures-for-chronicles-of-darkness?p=977615#post977615\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's the Quickstart for each 2E line that has one:<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/114063/Reap-the-Whirlwind?cPath=8329_20642\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a><br /> <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/118271/Demon-The-Descent-Quickstart?manufacturers_id=4261\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a><br /> <br /> Huh, I thought there were more of them? Guess not <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>I seriously had no idea those even existed, more proof to me that drivethru is garbage, I can't even find things I am interested in.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.pinterest.com/xenoterracide/chrod-inspirations/\" target=\"_blank\">Graphic Inspirational Photos for Chronicles of Darkness on Pinterest</a> <br /> <a href=\"https://chroniclesofdarkness.slack.com\" target=\"_blank\">Chronicles of Darkness Slack</a> (PM Me with Email for an Invite, then invite your friends)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4046-xenoterracide","name":"xenoterracide","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"563"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-28T09:03:34-07:00","id":977796,"title":"","content":"It's worth noting that the vampire one is just a port of an adventure from 1e, Into the Void.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-28T12:08:21-07:00","id":977880,"title":"","content":"I own The Harvesters and Nightmare At Hill Manor.<br /> <br /> Harvesters actually contains two unrelated adventures. The first (titular) adventure is more or less a straight crime story that happens to also have ghosts. The second adventure, Chicago Workings, is much weirder and also slots surprisingly well into a God Machine story if one so wanted.<br /> <br /> Nightmare At Hill Manor is designed as a one session survival horror game with a dash of investigation. I've run it a couple times and its pretty fun, if a little linear. One aspect of the story kind of gets left unexplained by the end, and while this could easily be used as a hook to start a longer game on its own my players have called it more of a plot hole.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-28T13:51:46-07:00","id":977953,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Nightmare At Hill Manor actually came to my mind after I didn't find any quickstart adventure for Chronicles of Darkness. Is it much work to convert it to CoD or can most mechanical related parts be mostly taken as written? Maybe somebody already did this and posted it somewhere on the internet?</span></span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-28T14:10:19-07:00","id":977964,"title":"","content":"I ran Nightmare at Hill Manor as a 2e game, and it went quite well. The ghost rules don't really translate very well, but it's easy to excuse as part of the unique nature of Hill's powers and his influence over the building. Other than that, everything is super easy to convert. I'll see if I still have my notes somewhere.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-28T15:15:47-07:00","id":977996,"title":"","content":"Nope, my notes are gone. But, looking over Hill Manor again, it looks like everything except the ghosts can just be directly ported over. Just remember to add their Athletics to Defense and to change weapon ratings to bonus damage instead of bonus dice. The ghosts don't take <i>too much</i> work to convert. Here's a pretty by-the-books version:<br /> <br /> Sullivain Barnes<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> Virtue: Patient<br /> Vice: Pessimistic<br /> Rank: 2 (Essence 15/15)<br /> Power: 4<br /> Finesse: 4<br /> Resistance: 3<br /> Corpus: 8<br /> Willpower: 7<br /> Integrity: 4<br /> Size: 5<br /> Speed: 13 (Species Factor 5)<br /> Defense: 4<br /> Initiative: 7<br /> Ban: Cannot leave Hill Manor<br /> Bane: Blessed Objects<br /> Influences: Regret 2<br /> Numina: Left-Handed Spanner, Sign<br /> Manifestations: Twilight Form, Fetter, Unfetter, Image<br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Josiah Hill<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> Virtue: Just<br /> Vice: Hateful<br /> Rank: 2 (Essence 15/15)<br /> Power: 5<br /> Finesse: 4<br /> Resistance: 5<br /> Corpus: 10<br /> Willpower: 9<br /> Integrity: 3<br /> Size: 5<br /> Speed: 14 (Species Factor 5)<br /> Defense: 4<br /> Initiative: 9<br /> Ban: Cannot leave Hill Manor<br /> Bane: Blessed Objects<br /> Influences: Revenge 2<br /> Numina: Awe, Dement<br /> Manifestations: Twilight Form, Fetter, Possess, Unfetter, Materialize<br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> You could give Hill unique Numina and/or Manifestations that more closely match his powers in the adventure, but I opted to just go for the best approximations from the standard Ephemeral Entity rules.<br /> <br /> The one change I would recommend making is to the &quot;Resisting the Compulsion&quot; action. I'd swap the whole thing out for resisting the Fetter Manifestation. And the blessed weapons Barnes gives the PCs should probably just count as a Bane for all the ghosts in the manor - they deal lethal to the possessed human, but aggravated to the possessing ghost.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-30T15:53:31-07:00","id":979300,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/977321-premade-adventures-for-chronicles-of-darkness?p=977996#post977996\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nope, my notes are gone. But, looking over Hill Manor again, it looks like everything except the ghosts can just be directly ported over....</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you very much for the info, much appreciated <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]}]}